\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Seed variance on devel (left) and test (right) for the two architectures. Horizontal lines are the means. On \emph  {test}, every single \texttt  {champ\_big} run beats the \emph  {best} champion run --- a +1.5 point mean improvement that survives seed variance.}}{17}{figure.caption.35}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:12-seed}{{13}{17}{Seed variance on devel (left) and test (right) for the two architectures. Horizontal lines are the means. On \emph {test}, every single \texttt {champ\_big} run beats the \emph {best} champion run --- a +1.5 point mean improvement that survives seed variance}{figure.caption.35}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Devel vs.\ test for every saved model in rounds 4--5. Pearson correlation is weak (and for \texttt  {champ\_big} even inverted): the worst-devel \texttt  {champ\_big\_s777} (67.6) has the \emph  {best} test (70.6), while the best-devel \texttt  {champ\_big\_s42} (70.7) has a middling test (69.1). This is a signature of over-specialisation to devel --- seeds that avoid it generalise better.}}{18}{figure.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:12-devtest}{{14}{18}{Devel vs.\ test for every saved model in rounds 4--5. Pearson correlation is weak (and for \texttt {champ\_big} even inverted): the worst-devel \texttt {champ\_big\_s777} (67.6) has the \emph {best} test (70.6), while the best-devel \texttt {champ\_big\_s42} (70.7) has a middling test (69.1). This is a signature of over-specialisation to devel --- seeds that avoid it generalise better}{figure.caption.36}{}}
